ProjectBlacklist: third-party notices
=====================================

Generated from licensing/sources.toml by `python -m licensing sync`.
Do not edit by hand.

Entries are suspected malicious or phishing hosts, not confirmed verdicts.

Build: all-in-one (GPL-3.0-only)
--------------------------------
complement plus redistributable third-party lists, for people who want a single URL.

* ProjectBlacklist curated data (CC0-1.0), https://github.com/JonathonPunc/ProjectBlacklist

* phishunt.io (CC0-1.0), https://phishunt.io/
  Condition: Describe entries as suspected, never as confirmed phishing (phishunt ToS sections 3 and 4).
  Condition: Don't misrepresent where the data came from (ToS section 4).
  Condition: Stay under 10 requests per second (ToS section 5).
  Requested: Credit phishunt.io when redistributing (ToS section 7: appreciated, not required).
  Requested: Send false-positive disputes to phishunt's GitHub issues with its false-positive template (ToS section 6).

* HaGeZi Threat Intelligence Feeds (GPL-3.0-only), https://github.com/hagezi/dns-blocklists
  Copyright HaGeZi and contributors. Published under the GNU General Public
  License v3.0; full text in LICENSE.
  Condition: A copy of the GPL-3.0 must accompany any redistribution (HaGeZi README, Redistribution and licensing).
  Condition: GPL-3.0 covers the list as HaGeZi publishes it, not the upstream feeds behind it; check those terms separately before using any of them directly.
  Requested: Fetch no more often than the list's Expires header says (8 hours when checked).
  Requested: Send false positives for TIF entries to https://github.com/hagezi/dns-blocklists/issues.

